# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the children TestDisableSignalExit
# starts (issue #417).
#
# This file exists because of a data race that is real, reproducible and
# not in this repository. rclone v1.75.0's lib/atexit publishes its signal
# channel in a plain package-level variable:
#
#   Register()       registerOnce.Do -> exitChan = make(...); go func() { sig := <-exitChan; ... }
#   IgnoreSignals()  signal.Stop(exitChan); close(exitChan); exitChan = nil
#
# The goroutine Register starts reads exitChan with no synchronisation
# against IgnoreSignals writing nil over it, so calling IgnoreSignals
# after something has already registered is an unsynchronised read/write
# pair on that variable. The detector reports it every time:
#
#   WARNING: DATA RACE
#   Write at 0x... by goroutine 21:
#     github.com/rclone/rclone/lib/atexit.IgnoreSignals()
#         lib/atexit/atexit.go:90
#     .../core/internal/transport/rclone.DisableSignalExit()
#         core/internal/transport/rclone/signalexit.go:35
#   Previous read at 0x... by goroutine 24:
#     github.com/rclone/rclone/lib/atexit.Register.func1.1()
#         lib/atexit/atexit.go:45
#
# It is reachable only in the order the "disabled-after" row exercises on
# purpose (register, then disable). cmd/backup-manager's daemon disables
# first, before any transfer, which never installs the handler and never
# writes the variable, so nothing in the shipped startup path provokes it.
# There is nothing to fix on this side either: the racing pair is two
# accesses to a variable in another module, with no synchronisation edge
# this repository can add between them.
#
# So the row keeps running, under the narrowest suppression that lets it:
# this one package in one module, and nothing else. TestDisableSignalExit
# asserts that it is matched exactly once, by the one row that provokes
# it, and matched by no other row. When rclone fixes this upstream that
# assertion goes red, which is the signal to delete this file rather than
# to carry a suppression nobody can remember the reason for.
race:github.com/rclone/rclone/lib/atexit
